# F3: outer profile under top cap F1: vertical wall loop F3 F5 F6 F4, top at z=20.0, base at z=0.0, material inside the loop (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F3_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
feature F3_Profile ProfileBoss(z=28.0, extent=28.0
    0.0 0.0
    0.0 80.0
    100.0 80.0
    100.0 0.0
)

# F7: outer profile under top cap F31: vertical wall loop F7 F9 F10 F8, top at z=28.0, base at z=20.0, material inside the loop; top edge beveled 1.0 deep at 90.0deg included (F21 F23 F24 F22) -- proposed as chamfer_depth, the loop read at the walls (CHECKLIST row 2.2)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F7_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# the top edge's 1.0mm bevel is the boss's chamfer_depth, at the included angle the
# model measures; a print that says otherwise is typed here (the three chamfer words are
# pick-two) -- break it with: run Form(tool=<ChamferMill>, surface=F7_Profile, comp=control, tip_clearance=...)
feature F7_Profile ProfileBoss(z=28.0, extent=8.0, chamfer_depth=1.0, chamfer_angle=90.0
    10.0 10.0
    10.0 30.0
    40.0 30.0
    40.0 10.0
)

# F19: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; flat floor F30 -- a milled bore; mouth bevel F2 absorbed, 1.0 deep at 90.0deg included -- extent runs to the virtual sharp corner (10.0); rim at z=20.0, 8.0 below the stock top z=28.0 -- authored from its rim by z=, so the step above it is another feature's material (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F19_Bore, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# a flat floor is milled, not drilled -- a twist drill leaves a conical point, so no drill run is suggested
# the mouth's 1.0mm bevel is the bore's chamfer_depth, at the included angle the
# model measures; a print that says otherwise is typed here (the three chamfer words are
# pick-two) -- break it with: run Form(tool=<ChamferMill>, surface=F19_Bore)
feature F19_Bore CylinderBore(dia=12.0, extent=10.0, x=70.0, y=60.0, z=20.0, chamfer_depth=1.0, chamfer_angle=90.0)

# F31: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F31_Top Plane(z=28.0)

# F32: pocket floor at z=12.0; vertical wall loop F25 F26 F28 F27, mouth at z=20.0, depth 8.0, opens upward; mouth beveled 1.0 deep at 90.0deg included (F11 F12 F13 F14) -- proposed as chamfer_depth, the mouth at the bevel's top (CHECKLIST row 2.1)
# consume with: run Clear(tool=..., profile=F32_Pocket, stepover=...)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# or finish with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F32_Pocket, comp=control)
# comp=control is required on recognized profile Side runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# the mouth's 1.0mm bevel is the pocket's chamfer_depth, at the included angle the
# model measures; a print that says otherwise is typed here (the three chamfer words are
# pick-two) -- break it with: run Form(tool=<ChamferMill>, surface=F32_Pocket)
feature F32_Pocket ProfilePocket(z=20.0, extent=8.0, chamfer_depth=1.0, chamfer_angle=90.0
    55.0 10.0
    85.0 10.0
    85.0 30.0
    55.0 30.0
)
